    "stdout": "ogent Makefile targets:\n\n  make all          - Run all lints and tests\n  make lint         - Run all linters (checkdoc, compile, package-lint)\n  make test         - Run all tests\n  make test-isolation - Verify the suite never writes real user stores\n  make offline-test - Replay workflows with real dependencies (OGENT_ELPA_DIR required)\n  make compile      - Byte-compile source files\n  make recompile    - Clean and compile; failures remain nonzero\n  make clean        - Remove generated lisp/ and test/ bytecode\n  make bench        - Run performance benchmarks\n  make batch        - Run Emacs in batch mode with project loaded\n  make interactive  - Run Emacs interactively with project loaded\n  make sandbox      - Run interactive Emacs in clean sandbox\n  make sandbox-test - Run tests in clean sandbox environment\n  make sandbox-lint - Run all linters in clean sandbox\n  make demo         - Launch demo.org in minimal Emacs\n\nOptions (pass as var=val):\n  v=1|2|3           - Verbosity level (-v, -vv, -vvv)\n  sandbox=1|DIR     - Run in sandbox mode\n  install-deps=1    - Auto-install package dependencies\n  install-linters=1 - Auto-install linting tools\n  debug=1           - Enable debug mode\n  EMACS=PATH        - Select the Emacs executable for every target\n\nExamples:\n  make test v=2                    - Run tests with verbose output\n  make lint sandbox=1              - Lint in clean sandbox\n  make all sandbox=1 install-deps=1 - Full CI-like run\n\nAdditional makem.sh rules (use make <rule>):\n  lint-checkdoc, lint-compile, lint-declare, lint-indent,\n  lint-package, lint-regexps, test-ert, test-buttercup\n\nAgent discovery (after loading ogent; no provider requests):\n  (ogent-agent-capabilities 'json) - Live tool contracts and approval policy\n  (ogent-agent-guide)             - Paste-ready SDK handbook\n  (ogent-agent-triage 'json)       - Discovery plus local health and next actions\n  (ogent-doctor-batch nil 'json)   - JSON health; exit 0 ok/info, 1 warning, 2 error\n",
